        "x1": 0.9073643790849674,
        "y1": 0.7072398989898989
      },
      "text": "To show that LI represents the Gâteaux derivative of J, let h ∈ L∞(0,T), ε > 0, and let define Iε = I + εh and let (pε,dε) = G(Iε) and (p,d) = G(I). Let define ΦI(ε) =",
